{
  "id": "Lyo.Algorithms.Postgres",
  "name": "Lyo.Algorithms.Postgres",
  "area": "Data",
  "tagline": "PostgreSQL catalog for Lyo.Algorithms. Schema algorithms, append-only revisions, labels.",
  "description": "IAlgorithmDefinitionStore on PostgreSQL. Tables algorithm_definition, algorithm_definition_revision, and algorithm_definition_label live in schema algorithms. Reads are AsNoTracking. SaveRevision locks the definition row, then allocates the next revision inside a transaction. Revision rows have an optional payload column for structured scorers. The store also implements IHealth.",
  "features": [
    "**Options.** PostgresAlgorithmOptions (section PostgresAlgorithms) extends PostgresOptionsBase. Schema is algorithms.",
    "**DI.** AddPostgresAlgorithmStore, the Action overload, and AddPostgresAlgorithmStoreFromConfiguration register the store and IHealth.",
    "**Migrations.** AddPostgresMigrations applies the schema when EnableAutoMigrations is true."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Register from configuration",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddAlgorithms();\nservices.AddPostgresAlgorithmStoreFromConfiguration(configuration);"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "When to use",
      "text": "Use this package when more than one process shares the catalog. SQLite is single-writer. Product tables keep their own algorithm key and optional revision or label; this schema stores the source."
    }
  ],
